course: dictionary
lesson: 11216
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it show you which one is meant. The word woo is a good example. «The prince tried to woo the princess with songs and gifts.» Here woo means to try to make someone love you.
explain: «The candidates woo voters before every election.» It is the same word, but now it means to try hard to get people's support. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then pick the meaning that fits.
explain: «Woo-hoo! We won the match!» Here woo is a cry of excitement, not a word about love or votes. The exclamation mark and the happy feeling are your clues. Always check the clues before you choose a meaning.
fact: Woo is a verb, so it changes: woo, woos, wooed, wooing.
fact: «Woo» can mean to try to make someone love you, or to try hard to get support, such as voters or customers.
fact: «Woo-hoo!» is a cry of excitement, like when your team scores a goal.
fact: Informal slang: «woo-woo» means ideas that are mystical and not backed by science.
fact: In Mandarin, wǔ («woo», said with a dip in the voice) means five, like five fingers spread. It is a different word from English woo.
exercise: «The prince tried to woo the princess with songs.» What does woo mean here? | To wake up early | *To try to make someone love you | To count to five | To shout with excitement
exercise: «The shop tried to woo customers with free cakes.» What does woo mean here? | To cry out in joy | To build a wooden fence | To be bored and tired | *To try hard to get people to choose you
exercise: «Woo-hoo! We won the race!» What is woo-hoo here? | A sad sigh | A name for a king | A word for the number five | *A cry of excitement
test: «The politicians wooed voters across the town.» What does wooed mean? | Walked slowly home | *Tried hard to win people's support | Painted the walls | Shouted at the sky
test: Mina says her friend's idea is pure woo. What does she mean? | Ideas that are five steps long | *Mystical ideas that are not backed by science | Ideas about cooking | Ideas that are very loud
exam: Which meaning of woo fits best in «The candidates wooed the crowd with promises»? | To cry out in joy | To count to five | *To try hard to get people's support | To fall asleep in a chair
